\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Superposition of the optical-laser and X-ray intensity profiles in the sample plane, with the smaller X-ray spot positioned inside the broader laser profile. This overlap is important because it ensures that the probed sample volume is excited while providing tolerance to the optical laser's spatial jitter.}}{13}{figure.caption.16}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:xary laser both}{{14}{13}{Superposition of the optical-laser and X-ray intensity profiles in the sample plane, with the smaller X-ray spot positioned inside the broader laser profile. This overlap is important because it ensures that the probed sample volume is excited while providing tolerance to the optical laser's spatial jitter}{figure.caption.16}{}}
